10:## §1 — OBSERVE
15:### 1.1 Catalogue mechanics (read firsthand)
18:- **Firsthand corrections to the digest prose (priced readings, binding on the build):** (1) The grid is **7 columns × 5 rows = 35 day numerals** (Persian numerals ۱–۳۵, right-to-left reading order), counted in ev/020 + census frames. (2) The "two ringed" lifecycle, CORRECTED at §2b under codex-observe (which re-read the frames cell-by-cell): a PLAIN ring first marks **day 16** (row 3, second cell from the right; census @17 s) and that SAME cell carries the ⊗ in ev/020 — the plain ring CONVERTS to ⊗ as the sweep passes it; it is not overstruck and there is NO separate day-23 ring (the builder's first reading misattributed the cell — cured here). The second ring marks **day 34** plain by 19 s and converts to ⊗ only in the final state (25 s). (3) In the final state ALL 35 cells are marked — day 35 (bottom-left) carries a diagonal slash in ev/026 (codex-observe's count: 35 marked incl. the two ⊗ cells); the builder's first reading ("day 35 never struck") is cured: the final strike target is 35, with day 35's slash landing in the final phase. (4) The timeline + star figure + dashed arc are ALREADY present at the first calendar frame (17 s) with ONE drop-line (from day 16) and its label UNSTRUCK; the second drop-line (from day 34), the first label's strike, and the second label arrive by 19 s. The digest's draw-on order (grid → strikes → drop-lines → timeline labels) is the CLAIM the build enforces for its own phases; the source's pre-assembled timeline/figure is named as set, not technique, in §2.2 deferrals. (5) The window head (13–17 s) is T242's bar chart and the tail (≥26.5 s) dissolves into the next scene (tiny population figures, panels dimming) — both are departures tabled in §2.3, not T243 lifecycle. (6) The figure's chest star CRACKS at 26 s — the next beat's opening glyph, deferred (§2.2). (7) Entrance anchor (codex-observe, firsthand): at source 16.5 s the calendar is partially drawn with first-row strikes visible; by 17.0 s it is assembled — the build's grid-phase expansion (§2.3 departure b) is priced against this anchor.
