60:## §2 — PLAN
62:### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
64:Derived (named, never stored): dayCount = cols×rows (=35; count assertion: source-count 35 = built-count 35, harness-printed) · day label of cell i = String(firstDay + i) · cellW = panelW/cols · cellH = panelH/rows · strike order = index order 0..dayCount−1 (RTL reading is a rendering direction; the sweep's index order is the priced allocation of the census's row-wise progression) · phase starts: gridStart=0 · strikes1Start=gridStart+gridDurMs (=1200) · dropStart=strikes1Start+strikes1DurMs (=3200) · labelsStart=dropStart+dropDurMs (=3800) · hold1End=labelsStart+labelsDurMs (=4400) · tasksStart=hold1End+hold1DurMs (=5400) · sweep3Start=tasksStart+tasksDurMs (=6400) · finalStart=sweep3Start+sweep3DurMs (=8400) · completeAtMs=finalStart+finalDurMs (=10400) · durationMs=completeAtMs+holdMs (=12400) · strikeFloat(t): 0 before strikes1Start; →strikes1Target across strikes1; →strikes2Target across tasks phase; →strikes3Target across sweep3; →strikesFinalTarget across final · cell i strikeP = clamp(strikeFloat − i, 0, 1) (ring cells' strikeP drives their ⊗ cross instead of a slash — a ring cell renders slash XOR cross, never both) · **ONE ring-cross authority (codex-plan-review cure): both ring crosses are their cell's strikeP** — ringEarly crossP = strikeP(ringEarlyIdx), ringLate crossP = strikeP(ringLateIdx); marked-cell counts (strikesFull) count cells by strikeP ≥ 1, ring cells included on the same term · ringEarly: plain ring forms across the last ringFormFraction (0.25) of grid phase · ringLate: plain ring forms across the last ringLateFormFraction (0.20) of strikes1 · drop1P = gridP (census: drop-line 1 is set at first calendar frame; it falls from ringEarly's cell — **drop 1 is pre-existing SET, outside the named order's scope**, see order-scope note below) · drop2P across drop phase (falls from ringLate's cell) · labelA: VISIBLE from gridP (timeline set, opacity = gridP); its strikeP + labelB opacity run across labels phase · labelB strikeP across final phase (both label strikes X-form per §1.4 (3), drawn from each label's strikeP) · arcOpacity = gridP × (1 − finalP) · tasksP across tasks phase (panel slides from x+tasksTravelPx with opacity; tasksTravelPx = panelW × tasksTravelRatio derived) · tasksRowsVisible = tasksRowsJoin during tasks phase, → tasksRowsTotal across sweep3; tasks row lines render tasksLineStyle ("dashed") once sweep3 begins, solid during the join (census CP8000 solid → CP10000 dashed — a phase-derived style, the key names the final treatment) · calShiftP = tasksP (calendar group translates −calShiftPx × tasksP) · cell x positions derive from readingDir ("rtl": index 0 at the panel's right edge; "ltr" mirrors) · **palette hierarchy by construction:** unstruck numerals render palette.ink, struck numerals palette.faint, marks (strikes/crosses/rings) palette.strike — the harness asserts the FAINT role (struck numerals, dimmer than the marks over them) stays distinct from both ink and strike under the palette swap (default ink == strike: the specimen is monochrome white; the separation the technique needs is struck-numeral vs mark, priced at the cure round before prewave). **Order scope (codex-plan-review cure):** the named draw-on order governs exactly: grid assembly → strikes sweep 1 → drop-line 2 → timeline-label events (A strike + B reveal). Drop-line 1, the timeline, label A's TEXT, the figure and the arc are pre-existing set arriving with the grid phase (the census's first calendar frame already carries them); sweeps 2–3 and the final phase intentionally run CONCURRENT with the tasks join and label B's strike (the census shows strikes continuing while the tasks panel joins) — concurrency there is census behaviour, not an order violation. Phase exclusivity is asserted where the order claims it: drop2P = 0 before dropStart · labelA strikeP = 0 and labelB opacity = 0 before labelsStart (harness P4/P5 pre-conditions). **Validation:** durations >0 finite; targets strictly increasing and ≤ dayCount (final target = dayCount: every cell marked in the final state, per the cured §1.1 (3)); ring indices distinct and < dayCount; **ringEarlyIdx < strikes1Target AND ringLateIdx ≥ strikes3Target AND ringLateIdx < strikesFinalTarget** (each conversion completes inside its designated sweep); tasksRowsJoin ≤ tasksRowsTotal; fractions in (0,1); **bounds (jev-plan-exit): cols/rows positive integers with cols ≤ 10 and rows ≤ 8 · two panels + gap fit the stage (2×panelW + tasksGapPx ≤ stageW) · panelY + panelH < timelineY · ringRPx < min(cellW, cellH)/2 + ringRPx margin priced (ring may exceed the cell — census rings overlap neighbours slightly; the bound is ringRPx ≤ cellW, asserted)**; a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered (harness validator receipts: ring-index-out-of-range rejected · panel-overflow rejected).
66:### 2.2 Construction choice
70:**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Window head (source 13–17 s, T242's bars) — outside this technique; the allocation discards it (departure table §2.3). (2) The figure's chest-star crack at 26 s — the next beat's glyph; the build holds the final state. (3) The tail transition (≥26.5 s: dimming panels, tiny population figures) — next scene, not built. (4) The "perhaps…" annotation at 23 s — caption-adjacent scene text, not technique; not built. (5) Persian numeral glyphs + Persian label texts — the build renders CONFIG Latin strings (numerals derived from firstDay, labels as CONFIG text); the technique is the order + marks, not the specimen's language — the swap test re-labels freely, which is the parameterization proof. (6) The source's calendar entrance is unobserved (inside the 15→17 s gap): the build's grid phase is an ALLOCATION expanding that entrance so the named order reads — priced in §2.5, departure-tabled in §2.3. (7) The figure's lateral drift in the source (it tracks the calendar's shift and recentres by the final state) is simplified to a FIXED figureCx — the drop-lines land on the timeline at CONFIG-derived x positions in both readings; the drift is staging, not technique.
72:### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
74:**Departure table:** (a) census CP0/CP2000 (seg-rel 0/2000, T242 bars) have NO build counterpart (deferral 1). (b) Census CP4000 (seg-rel 4000) shows the panel ASSEMBLED with 7 strikes already — the build expands the entrance: its grid phase (0–1200) draws panel+numerals with 0 strikes, so the build reaches "grid complete" at 1200 where the census has it at seg-rel 4000; every later anchor is then offset by the build's own phase durations, and the mapping below binds build states to census STATES (not to raw seg-rel arithmetic). (c) Census CP14000 (seg-rel 14000, transition out) has no build counterpart (deferral 3); the build's final hold stands in its place.
75:**State mapping (build instant → census state it must equal):** build 4400 (labels end) ≡ CP6000 state (strikes 20 · ringEarly ⊗ · ringLate plain · drops 2 · labelA struck · labelB present unstruck · tasks absent) · build 5400 (hold1 end) ≡ CP7000 state (identical — the hold) · build 6400 (tasks end) ≡ CP8000 state (tasks 3 rows · strikes 26 · calendar shifted) · build 8400 (sweep3 end) ≡ CP10000 state (tasks 5 rows · strikes 32) · build 10400 (final end) ≡ CP12000 state (strikes 35 — all cells marked · ringLate ⊗ · labelB struck · arc 0) · build 11400 (hold mid) ≡ CP12000 state (full-state equality, crack deferred).
